                        ],
                        "form": "го́рничных"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fce3d599-de3a-38e3-b764-b0ce3930a2a0",
                        "entry_id": "588d0160-e84b-301c-9002-a9afc08ba230",
                        "glosses": [
                            "женщина, в обязанности которой входит уборка номеров в гостинице"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9146d21c-f907-4dc5-98c9-e842bcd84f2e",
                                "sense_id": "fce3d599-de3a-38e3-b764-b0ce3930a2a0",
                                "text": "— Необходимо сокращать сроки обучения! Чтобы научить работе горничной, не нужны четыре года: научиться улыбаться можно за два месяца! — обозначила на слушаниях в Совете Федерации новый стратегический курс спикер верхней палаты Валентина Матвиенко."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "37110781-e096-3db4-aea9-4b6a89f93b85",
                        "entry_id": "588d0160-e84b-301c-9002-a9afc08ba230",
                        "glosses": [
                            "служанка при госпоже/господине"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9f06dc4-80d4-4ec3-9514-5f4cfa0508da",
                                "sense_id": "37110781-e096-3db4-aea9-4b6a89f93b85",
                                "text": "Правда, несколько месяцев назад мы уже успокоились и решили, что всё опять наладится: Брайтон обручился с Рэчел Хауэлз, нашей младшей горничной."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b287fc4c-4f3c-42af-91ff-354317e2dd3c",
                        "source_entry_id": "588d0160-e84b-301c-9002-a9afc08ba230",
                        "target_lang_word": "maid",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "maid",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc01c78b-528b-3541-974d-da26bee76c15",
                                        "entry_id": "6e61b0a2-9dcc-37cc-adfb-4450f692c91d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A girl or an unmarried young woman; maiden."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "poetic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e56c409e-22d2-364a-9103-4dbf81541532",
                                        "entry_id": "6e61b0a2-9dcc-37cc-adfb-4450f692c91d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female servant or cleaner (short for maidservant)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99b46aec-2cf0-4111-8c95-0fbe9d3894e8",
                                                "sense_id": "e56c409e-22d2-364a-9103-4dbf81541532",
                                                "text": "She was a fat, round little woman, richly apparelled in velvet and lace, […]; and the way she laughed, cackling like a hen, the way she talked to the waiters and the maid,[…]—all these unexpected phenomena impelled one to hysterical mirth, and made one class her with such immortally ludicrous types as Ally Sloper, the Widow Twankey, or Miss Moucher."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74b3538b-2068-329f-b957-70de9138fe43",
                                        "entry_id": "6e61b0a2-9dcc-37cc-adfb-4450f692c91d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A virgin, now female but originally one of either gender."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e970cb51-c3f9-440f-8ab3-8fc95fc25aaf",
                                                "sense_id": "74b3538b-2068-329f-b957-70de9138fe43",
                                                "text": "You are betrothed both to a maid and man."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "07c0475b-2b7f-4157-86b3-56354204098b",
